{"name":"Gosling","hex":"#857668","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Gosling","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Gosling"}],"entries":[{"title":"Goose","blocks":[{"text":"A goose is a bird of any of several waterfowl species in the family Anatidae. This group comprises the genera Anser and Branta. Some members of the Tadorninae subfamily are commonly called geese, but are not considered \"true geese\" taxonomically. More distantly related members of the family Anatidae are swans, most of which are larger than true geese, and ducks, which are smaller."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Anser_anser_1_%28Piotr_Kuczynski%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Anser_anser_1_%28Piotr_Kuczynski%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goose","wikidata":"Q16529344"},{"title":"Gosling (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Gosling is an English surname. Notable people with the surname include:"},{"items":["Armine Nutting Gosling (1861–1942), Newfoundland women's rights activist","Sir Audley Charles Gosling (1836–1913), British diplomat","Charles Gosling (1868–1917), British Army officer","Clint Gosling, New Zealand footballer","Dan Gosling, English footballer","R. Cunliffe Gosling (1868–1922), nineteenth century England football captain","Harry Gosling (1861–1930), British politician and trade union leader","Jake Gosling, English producer and songwriter","Jake Gosling, British footballer","James Gosling, Canadian software developer, considered father of Java","Joanna Gosling, British journalist","John Gosling (disambiguation)","John Gostling (1644–1733), English singer","Julia Gosling, Canadian ice hockey player","Katelyn Gosling, Canadian ice hockey player","Lewis Gosling, British trampoline gymnast","Luke Gosling, Australian politician","Mark Gosling (1886–1980), Australian painter and politician","Mike Gosling, United States former Major League Baseball pitcher","Nicole Gosling, Canadian ice hockey player","Paula Gosling, English crime writer","Ray Gosling (1939–2013), English television presenter, journalist and gay rights activist","Raymond Gosling (1926–2015), English scientist","Richard Gosling, English strongman","Ryan Gosling, Canadian actor","Simon Gosling, British modeller and propmaker","William Gosling (1892–1945), English recipient of the Victoria Cross","William Gosling, British electrical engineer","William Gilbert Gosling (1863–1930), Newfoundland politician, businessman, and author","William Gosling (footballer) (1869–1952), British footballer","William W. Gosling (1824–1883), English landscape painter"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gosling_(surname)","wikidata":"Q16870259"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg/500px-Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg/1280px-Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg/500px-Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Snow geese (Anser caerulescens) in Quebec, Canada","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/B%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG/500px-B%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/B%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG/1280px-B%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG?utm_source=en.wiki